# logs-gateway

Spring Boot 3.4 / Java 21 service: ingest logs over HTTP, mask PAN, route to Kafka, index app logs in OpenSearch, archive audit logs to S3.

## Current state (do not regress)

- Base package: `com.bank.observability.logsgateway`. Main class: `LogsGatewayApplication`.
- Package-by-feature is live: `ingest/`, `masking/`, `routing/`, `audit/`, `appindex/`, `config/`, `shared/`.
- Feature packages use `api/`, `domain/`, `infrastructure/` as needed. `domain/` never imports `api/` or `infrastructure/`.
- Tests live under the same package path as `src/main`. Keep tests green after every move.

## Ingest contract (never break)

- `POST /v1/logs/ingest` requires `traceId`, `serviceName`, `logType`.
- Missing fields → `400`. Valid payload → `202 Accepted`. Fire-and-forget.
- `AUDIT` → Kafka `bank.logs.audit` → S3. All other types → `bank.logs.app` → OpenSearch.
- Kafka partition key = `traceId`.

## Conventions

- Java 21 records for DTOs and the internal envelope; no Lombok going forward.
- Kafka producer: `acks=all`, `enable.idempotence=true`. Consumers: manual ack after downstream success; poison → `*.DLT`.
- PAN masking: Luhn-aware, at most first-6 + last-4. CVV must never be logged.
- Tests mirror `src/main`. Run `mvn verify` after each step (`mvn test -Dgroups=it` for Kafka Testcontainers IT).

```java
// Edge DTO: Jakarta validation on the HTTP record
public record IngestLogRequest(
    Instant timestamp,
    @NotBlank String serviceName,
    @NotBlank String traceId,
    String logLevel,
    @NotBlank String logType,
    String message,
    Map<String, Object> data) {}
```
